  "findings": [
    "Reads keep up on Kubernetes to 3000 rps with p99 9.1 ms at 0.23 cores and 0 throttled periods, the same shape as compose (p99 15.1 ms).",
    "Read 5000 sits on the edge: the recorded pass held 4996.8 rps (p99 50.7 ms, 0.46 cores, 37 throttled periods); a first pass was OOM-killed twice (3517.9 rps, 17 809 dropped, 44 575 errors).",
    "Writes are bounded by the pg pool of 10: write 1000 reaches 837.8 rps with 2883 waiting at 0.19 cores, the ~800 rps knee compose showed.",
    "Past the write knee the api is OOM-killed twice per run (write 2000, 3000, 5000 and mixed 3000). Kubernetes restarts it within the run, so requests fail fast (p50 187.2 to 187.6 ms and max in flight 4497 to 4910 at write 2000, 3000 and mixed 3000, against 10 000 on compose) and achieved rps counts those failures: goodput is 272, 231 and 90 rps for write 2000, 3000, 5000 and 355 rps for mixed 3000.",
    "Mixed 1000 is fine (p99 18.2 ms). Every error in the matrix has no HTTP status and falls in a run where the api was OOM-killed, so none is attributed to the NodePort path; the NodePort did reset connections for up to ~100 s after each kill while the pod was Ready, which is why runs were gated on clean health probes and why stats samples are missing in killed runs."
  ],
